{0 rewards-core}

Loyalty points for banks as pure values and state machines: an append-only points
ledger per customer, earn rules for settled card spend, one-off action bonuses, tiers
over a rolling window, cashback redemption booked through [ledger], an expiry policy
and points statements. Nothing here persists or opens a connection; a service keeps the
entries and redemptions behind {!Rewards_core.Store.S}.

{1 Where to start}

- {!Rewards_core.Program}: the configuration of a programme (earn rules, tiers,
  cashback, expiry).
- {!Rewards_core.Engine}: the operations (settle a purchase, refund, bonus, adjust,
  expire, redeem) over any store and monad.
- {!Rewards_core.Points_account} and {!Rewards_core.Entry}: the ledger rules (balance
  never negative, one entry per cause).
- {!Rewards_core.Earn_rules}, {!Rewards_core.Clawback_rule}, {!Rewards_core.Tiers},
  {!Rewards_core.Cashback},
  {!Rewards_core.Expiry}: the pure rules.
- {!Rewards_core.Booking}: the cash entry for a completed redemption.
- {!Rewards_core.Summary} and {!Rewards_core.Statement}: what a customer sees.
- {!Rewards_core.Store_memory} and {!Rewards_core.Store_conformance}: an in-memory store
  and the scenarios any store must pass.

{1 Example}

[examples/quickstart.ml] in the repository runs a small programme from purchases to a
booked cashback; [dune test] checks its output.
